            <div xml:id="d424">

                <pb facs="0526" n="414" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg414"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 24354/14.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Costa Rican Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-08"><hi rendition="#italic">June 8,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 25th ultimo, in which you express the profound gratitude of
                    the Government of Costa Rica for the various proofs of consideration and good
                    will given by the legislative and executive branches of the Government of the
                    United States, the American National Red Cross, and the American people, in the
                    hour of sorrow and grief which the calamity at Cartago has occasioned.</p>
                <p>In compliance with your request the department will take pleasure in making known
                    to the parties interested the contents of your note,</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">P. C. Knox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
